      "source_line_start": 565,
      "source_line_end": 583,
      "current_tex": "\\begin{lemma}[Integer Ceiling Lemma]\n\\label{lem:integer-ceiling-lemma}\nFor every $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$, there exists a unique $m\\in\\mathbb{Z}$ such that\n\\[\n  m-1<x\\leq m.\n\\]\nEquivalently,\n\\[\n  (\\forall x\\in\\mathbb{R})(\\exists!m\\in\\mathbb{Z})(m-1<x\\leq m).\n\\]\nThe unique integer $m$ is denoted by\n\\[\n  m=\\lceil x\\rceil.\n\\]\n\n\\smallskip\n\\noindent\n\\hyperref[prf:integer-ceiling-lemma]{\\textit{Go to proof.}}\n\\end{lemma}",
      "formalizations": []
    }
  },
